  title="Geometry & Arrows"
  description="The BBox value object, one-call text and shape helpers, and real arrows with auto-routed endpoints."
>
  <p class="lead">
    The v2.8 geometry layer collapses the historical seven-line styling ritual into single calls,
    and gives you a proper value object for rectangular regions.
  </p>

  <h2 id="bbox">BBox — the region value object</h2>
  <Code code={snippet0} />
  <p>
    <code>BBox</code> splats into every <code>add_*</code> call (<code>*bb</code> expands to
    left, top, width, height). Float arithmetic on lengths is coerced at the setter, so
    expressions like <code>(Inches(10) - gutter) / 2</code> are safe.
  </p>

